@@ -197,7 +197,20 @@ EduLens is fully configured for **serverless deployment on Vercel** out-of-the-b
 
 ### How It Works on Vercel
 - **Serverless API (`api/index.py`):** Fast, stateless Python functions running on Vercel Serverless Functions. Handles real-time ML inference (`/api/predict`), curriculum analytics (`/api/topics`), benchmark samples (`/api/samples`), and model health (`/api/health`).
-- **Interactive Web App (`public/index.html`):** Modern, lightweight, responsive client dashboard powered by Tailwind CSS, Chart.js, and Lucide icons.
+- **Interactive Web App (`public/`):** A simple, student-friendly dashboard built with plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript (no build step, no CDN frameworks).
+  - `public/index.html` – page shell, icons and dialogs
+  - `public/assets/styles.css` – design tokens (light/dark), layout and components
+  - `public/assets/app.js` – hash router, API client and the six views
+
+  **Navigation:** Overview · My Sessions · My Progress · Quizzes (main) and Connect & Ingest · Settings (secondary). The *Ingest session* action is available from the top bar on every page.
+
+  **Data accuracy rules the UI follows:** topic understanding (ML prediction), actual quiz score (deterministic grading), expressed confidence (wording signals) and overall topic score are shown separately. Missing values are shown as "Quiz not attempted", "Awaiting quiz" or "Not enough data yet" and are never replaced by a fallback number; charts leave gaps instead of inventing points; catalogue topics are never counted as studied.
+
+  **Run locally:**
+  ```bash
+  uvicorn api.index:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload
+  # open http://127.0.0.1:8000/  (health check: /api/health)
+  ```
 - **Fast & Lightweight:** Unnecessary training datasets are excluded via `.vercelignore`, making deployment zip bundles ultra-compact (< 2MB).
 
 ### Deploy in 2 Steps:
